mbent Frank J. Mrvan (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Northwest Indiana's first district is only slightly Democratic on paper, but incumbent Frank Mrvan enters the general election with strong structural advantages. He has matched his Republican challenger in fundraising, holds incumbent benefits, and has spent the fall on visible constituent work, from utility-cost legislation to disaster-declaration support. Pete Buttigieg's campaign visit underscores Democratic confidence in the seat.\n\nRepublican Barb Regnitz has run a serious campaign, raising about $2.4 million and holding a cash-on-hand edge, and she carries Donald Trump's endorsement. Still, expert raters overwhelmingly place the race at Safe or Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Mrvan's chances near 97%. With no public polling available, the forecast rests on fundamentals and ratings, both of which point to a comfortable Mrvan win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9569, "margin": 11.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9243, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9241, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9308, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9246, "margin": 10.6}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9079, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9227, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9206, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9443, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.938, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9373, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9482, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9254, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9274, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9315, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9183, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9321, "margin": 10.8}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9084, "margin": 9